{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1417526-what-do-you-need-to-be-a-solar-crafter","id":1417526,"title":"What do you need to be a (Solar) crafter?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-10T02:43:11-07:00","id":1417526,"title":"What do you need to be a (Solar) crafter?","content":"Hello all, I was wondering if anyone has looked over and figured out which of the more than 50+ charms a Supernal Crafter would reliably need to begin crafting as it seems very excessive to me (12 charms)?<br /> <br /> <b>Charms Needed</b><br /> 1) 6 from Efficiency for Tireless Workhorse Method, Efficient Craftsman Technique, Arete Shifting Prana, Sublime Transference, Ages Echoing Wisdom, Dragon Soul Emergence<br /> -This gets you a total of 5 major slots, 1 superior slot, 5 gold experience every story. <br /> <br /> 2) 5 from power for Flawless Handiwork Method x 2, Triumph Forging Eye, Experiential Conjuring of the true void, First Movement of the Demiurge<br /> -This gives you rerolls for 10's, and 6's, maximum dice, +1 free success, +1 dice, and for every 3 successes that match numbers you get 2.55 successes, and due to the number for a maximum dice pool per roll this gives you an average of 18 or so successes. <br /> <br /> 3) Craftsman Needs No Tools...<br /> <br /> <b>Results</b><br /> This basically means with those charms, you will need 30 gold experience as you should be able to complete the task within 3 rolls, and 18 weeks? Unfortunately you are a complete failure at any thing related to staying alive since you are going to have maybe 1 ox body technique, and 2 combat charms? In comparison you need maybe 4 charms to become an extremely powerful character with any other non-combat skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T02:46:58-07:00","id":1417527,"title":"","content":"My crafter started with Craftsman Needs No Tools and Durability-Enhancing Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T02:53:46-07:00","id":1417528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1417526-what-do-you-need-to-be-a-solar-crafter?p=1417527#post1417527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My crafter started with Craftsman Needs No Tools and Durability-Enhancing Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but doesn't that mean you likely took a massive load of experience just to get to a high enough dice pool, to make them faster than more than 36 weeks and that is just for level 2 Artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T04:17:08-07:00","id":1417531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1417526-what-do-you-need-to-be-a-solar-crafter?p=1417528#post1417528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting but doesn't that mean you likely took a massive load of experience just to get to a high enough dice pool, to make them faster than more than 36 weeks and that is just for level 2 Artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a leading question.<br /> <br /> That said, <i>no</i>, I didn\u2019t take \u201ca massive load of XP\u201d to make artifacts because, by and large, I wasn\u2019t worried about making artifacts. My character made dresses, slippers, tapestries, lingerie, dickies, doilies, gloves, hats, scarves, handkerchiefs, and deadly tripwire traps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T04:49:32-07:00","id":1417532,"title":"","content":"Yeah. If you want to rush Artifact crafting ASAP? It's going to be a lot of Charms.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a kick-ass craftsperson in a mundane craft who may or may not ever get into Artifacts? You can start with a lot less.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ages-Echoing Wisdom and Dragon Soul Emergence are nice, but not necessary as there are faster ways to generate cxp. Sublime Transference is the only Efficiency Charm you really want to start with ASAP so you can move your cxp around. Though Supreme Celestial Focus is also a good one to start with because:<br /> <br /> With it you can get up to Supreme Perfection of Craft from the Momentum tree and you're going to start drowning in cxp. This should average you 10 silver and 2 gold at the end of every story, and 3 silver and 1 gold at the end of every significant day that goes by per Craft at 5. Plus CNNT, and the earlier Momentum Charms for even more cxp. Supreme Celestial Focus also means you can raise additional Craft Abilities with gold cxp rather than having to toss lots of starting dots/XP at it. And don't forget your mundane cxp per story just for using your Crafts.<br /> <br /> From the Power tree... repurchasing Flawless Handiwork at start is minimally worth it. Bright Forging-Prana is worth two other Charms/repurchases as it i, so snag that over three other Charms from Power. Triumph-Forging Eye is great for anything you need lots of time for, since you can just take a few extra days and do one big roll each day.<br /> <br /> It's still a lot of Charms.. but RAW Crafts is annoying like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T05:23:56-07:00","id":1417535,"title":"","content":"You only need 6 Charms to spit out N/A artifacts:<br /> <br /> 1. Flawless handiwork <br /> 2-3. Supreme Masterwork x2<br /> 4. First movement of the Demiurge<br /> 5. Experimental Conjuring of the void<br /> 6. Bright-forging 1-Flawless handiwork 2 -Supreme masterwork 3 -Divine Inspiration Technique<br /> <br /> That gets you to an average of 425 successes on six rolls at Difficulty 5. (Math: <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/8nioxo/craft_system_3rd_edition_why_people_went_crazy/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/com...le_went_crazy/</a>)<br /> <br /> Realistically, in 2E Craft was all about Artifacts. In 3E, not so much. Mundane Craft is very central now. To build artifacts, you need to build other, useful, mundane things first. So as a Crafter... 90% of your time is building useful mundane things.<br /> <br /> Artifacts are a pretty sweet 10% bene, but not essential.<br /> <br /> I'd take Craftsman Needs No Tools, Durability Enhancing Technique, Shattering Grasp and two purchases of Flawless Handiwork Method on a Supernal Crafter. A few Presence Charms to sell my goods, an Ox-body, some combat Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1417526-what-do-you-need-to-be-a-solar-crafter#post1417526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately you are a complete failure at any thing related to staying alive since you are going to have maybe 1 ox body technique, and 2 combat charms? In comparison you need maybe 4 charms to become an extremely powerful character with any other non-combat skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Zeus, what are you fighting?<br /> <br /> Two combat Charms and an Ox-body is enough to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">defeat a fierce pirate captain in a duel, fight off magical flying sharks, then slay a dreaded manticore</a>. It's <i>nearly</i> enough to solo <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1380906#post1380906\">an elite Dragon-Blooded warrior trained to kill Solars</a>.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd recommend 5 Charms (including Ox-bodies) geared to keeping you alive, but 3 isn't awful.<br /> <br /> One Charm, Craftsman Needs No Tools, gives you extremely powerful crafting ability. More powerful than any mundane endeavour gets on four Charms (except maybe Sail, which is freakin' bonkers on four Charms). The Solar with CNNT is better at Craft than the Solar with 4 Presence Charms is at convincing folks to do stuff. Because Craft is more than just Crafting Artifacts, just like Presence is more than seducing a sexless, genderless, golem. If you want to seduce a genderless golem, Solar Presence lets you do that, but you need more than four Charms and that's not what Solar Presence is for -- it's a very small part of what Solar Presence can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-11-2020, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T05:55:52-07:00","id":1417539,"title":"","content":"For some info on how well 1-4 charm investments into craft power do at crafting different levels of artifacts, I wrote a program to simulate a bunch of rolls.<br /> All assume attribute 5, ability 5, a specialty, a full excellency, a 1-point stunt, 1 willpower/roll, essence 1 but craft supernal, and no other bonuses.<br /> Probabilities are rounded to whole percentage points.<br /> 1 charm: only choice is Flawless Handiwork method, 100% chance of artifact 2, 94% of artifact 3, 16% of artifact 4.<br /> 2 charms:<br /> FHM x2: 100% chance of artifact 2, 99% of artifact 3, 48% of artifact 4, 1% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM, Supreme Masterwork Focus: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 68% of artifact 4, 4% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM, Experiential Conjuring of True Void: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 81% of artifact 4, 9% chance of artifact 5.<br /> 3 charms:<br /> FHM x2, SMF: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 92% of artifact 4, 25% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM x2, EC: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 98% of artifact 4, 40% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM, SMFx2: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 95% of artifact 4, 38% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM, SMF, ECoTV: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 99% of artifact 4, 63% chance of artifact 5.<br /> FHM, ECoTV, First Movement of the Demiurge: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 100% of artifact 4, 100% chance of artifact 5, 10% chance of artifact NA.<br /> 4 charms: give the success of First Movement of the Demiurge, I'll only test with that<br /> FHMx2, ECoTV, FMotD: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 100% of artifact 4, 100% chance of artifact 5, 47% chance of artifact NA.<br /> FHM, SMF, ECoTV, FMotD: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 100% of artifact 4, 100% chance of artifact 5, 32% chance of artifact NA.<br /> FHM, ECoTV, FMotD, Unbroken Image Focus: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 100% of artifact 4, 100% chance of artifact 5, 96% chance of artifact NA.<br /> <br /> Conclusion - unless you want to try for artifact NA, you really only need flawless handiwork method, experiential conjuring of true void, and first movement of the demiurge.<br /> <br /> a note - at essence 2, non-supernal, those charms get you: 100% chance of artifact 2, 100% of artifact 3, 99.7% of artifact 4, 93.1% chance of artifact 5, .5% chance of artifact NA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T13:52:18-07:00","id":1417569,"title":"","content":"Or, in other words, the Power tree is one of the worst in the Solar Craft bloat, because it's 3x as large as it needs to be to do its main job, and you're not even getting some neat high level stuff at the top that does cool stuff; just more dice/terminus/dice-tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T20:04:53-07:00","id":1417586,"title":"","content":"if you want to make Artifacts on the sly you can rush for <b>Vice Miracle Technique</b> (and its repurchase) to pull a Deus Ex Machina out of your (literal) pocket. I get a LOT of mileage out of that charm, i've used it to make a ring of good health, a serpentine sword belt, and and essence glider dracula bat cape. Just open the book to the minor artifacts section and you get one of those free per story, and Artifact 3 covers weapons and armor so as long as you got something coking in the kitchen you have basically a free artifact whenever you need it. This, plus the ever useful <b>Craftsmen Need No Tools</b> make you Johnny on the Spot with regards to most occasions where you will use craft in story. If you grab the next charm, <b>Words as Workshop Method</b>, you've basically solved every &quot;Twilight&quot; type problem of Craft, Medicine, and Investigate by having the Bat Utility Belt full of plot conveniences. If you toss in <b>Ever Ready Innovation Discipline</b> (its in Miracles of the Solar Exalted) then you have even more potential to just retcon away almost all of your crafting needs.<br /> <br /> Since I got these 4 charms, I almost never even need use the craft system the way its designed. Once you have the Craft XP charms you just surf this wave of cxp that you spend on getting more cxp like cookie clicker excpet for artifacts. I've bought more than ten craft abilities this way. I save 15 sxp for <b>ERID</b> and I convert the rest into Gold and then buy new crafts with them. When it comes time to actually, y'know, <i>make</i> something, the handful of Power charms listed above absolutely crush it. But honestly I only make things with my big old bucket of dice when i feel like doing it on a whim, because once everyone in the party has an artifact there's next to nothing left to make that isn't covered by <b>CNNT </b>and <b>VMT</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1417526-what-do-you-need-to-be-a-solar-crafter?p=1417569#post1417569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, in other words, the Power tree is one of the worst in the Solar Craft bloat, because it's 3x as large as it needs to be to do its main job, and you're not even getting some neat high level stuff at the top that does cool stuff; just more dice/terminus/dice-tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite my love of Vice Miracle Technique, there's literally no other reason to go into the Project Slots tree. It's useless. Unless you are building a Warship AND Artifact at the same time you will never hurt for project slots and I only remember they exist when it comes time to get free xp for having them. They're also reduced to a sidenote in my Dice Math cheat sheet for how much i need to spend on build projects. The whole idea of project slots is silly and exists just as a Charm Tax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 10-10-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T21:33:03-07:00","id":1417593,"title":"","content":"The Efficiency Tree has plenty of potential, and plenty of bloat. The point though, is that Power doesn't have high level Charms that you can at least be happy to have despite the inane number of Charms to get there.<br /> <br /> Otherwise... we don't need to have another round of &quot;why Solar Craft sucks.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}